# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and runs its CI on Ubuntu. Without this,
# git stores whatever the editor produced, and a CRLF file whose content is a
# shell script breaks on the runner in a way that reads as nonsense: the
# trailing \r becomes part of the last argument, so a `run: |` block fails with
# `$'\r': command not found` and a .sh hook fails on a line that looks correct.
#
# Everything textual is normalised to LF in the repository. Checkout on Windows
# is unaffected for ordinary source files; the entries below are the ones that
# are *executed* by something other than Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly LF — these are read by Linux runners, containers, or the OS image.
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.mjs      text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers keep CRLF, or cmd.exe mis-parses them.
*.bat      text eol=crlf
*.ps1      text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.ico      binary
*.pdf      binary
*.wasm     binary
*.zkey     binary
*.img      binary
